{"id": "9aa1dea7-8527-4591-8754-c5f9bd69cd67", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T02:46:54.124284", "source": "user", "parent_id": "fc9fbfd6-0f7c-4d14-8635-df71bff2cce3", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"This is a design-only task. Please report (1) what you find in /workspace and any provided context (e.g., track.md), to the extent relevant, (2) a proposed approach — high-level experiment design skeleton only, not a full protocol — for the question: does a Safety System Prompt (SSP) significantly enhance LLM robustness against jailbreak attacks, in terms of Attack Success Rate (ASR) under token-level and prompt-level attacks? The design must include at least: research question and hypotheses, independent variables (SSP on/off; attack family ∈ {token-level, prompt-level}), dependent variable (ASR definition and how refusal/jailbreak success is judged), candidate base model(s) and rationale, candidate attack methods (paired comparisons across token-level and prompt-level families, e.g., GCG-style suffix/token perturbation vs. prompt-level jailbreak templates), candidate SSP content shape (consistent with study_context setup_8 vs setup_9), datasets/prompts (benign and harmful prompt sources), controls and confounds (model version, decoding, system prompt ordering/placement, prompt template, attack budget, prompt length), replication/sample-size plan, analysis plan (per-cell ASR with CIs, paired statistical tests across SSP on/off within attack family, effect sizes, attack-family × SSP interaction), threats to validity, and feasibility given network disabled, no GPU, and no preinstalled dependencies. Do NOT run experiments, fabricate results, or write the full protocol yet. Also list (3) consequential assumptions you are making and (4) key uncertainties that require researcher/clinician judgement before I approve the approach. Stop after these four items; I will issue a focused follow-up before the full design.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Does incorporating a Safety System Prompt (SSP) significantly enhance the robustness of Large Language Models (LLMs) against jailbreak attacks? Specifically, how does the presence of SSP influence the Attack Success Rate (ASR) under both token-level and prompt-level attacks?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [\"neurips2024/97431/5:setup_8\", \"neurips2024/97431/5:setup_9\"], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
