{"id": "8e370241-d03c-4328-8945-54d6c2162f3b", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T02:51:10.493858", "source": "user", "parent_id": "fc940ec7-a3d8-43f7-8e1d-01fa3928b676", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Approach is approved. Resolutions to your remaining 5 uncertainties, to be respected verbatim in the final design: (U1) Token-count match — your default is accepted: a generic style/tone/formatting neutral preamble is auto-tuned with the Llama-3 tokenizer so its token-count matches the setup_9 safety preamble to within ≤1 token; report the two token counts and the diff in an appendix. (U2) Commit-hash pins — use the official registry defaults: meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct and meta-llama/Llama-Guard-3-8B; pin by the resolved commit hash at the moment of run and print it in the methods section. (U3) κ calibration slice — use HarmBench's labeled 'validation' split if present (≥50 examples); otherwise a deterministic held-out slice of 50 from HarmBench 'test' that is verified disjoint from the 400-behavior primary prompt set and from the JailbreakBench 100; report κ and a confusion matrix; do NOT threshold on κ. (U4) OMIT the 'whole-prompt editable' token-level sensitivity cell; the threat model is fixed to user-message-only editable. (U5) KEEP cell C17 (CPU smoke-test addendum) in the protocol as DEFERRED TO A DIFFERENT ENVIRONMENT with an explicit 'not in this sandbox' note; do not claim execution. Now produce the FINAL EXPERIMENT DESIGN deliverable as a single self-contained document with: (1) Title, research question, and the three pre-registered hypotheses; (2) Final SSP texts for setup_8 (length-matched neutral) and setup_9 (the ≤8-line safety preamble from §2.4) with a placeholder injection point for the token-count match; (3) Frozen design parameters (model + hash placeholder, judge + hash placeholder, HarmBench 400 + JailbreakBench 100, greedy T=0, user-message-only adversary, mult